Comment (internal/service/worker/dashboard_suggestion_worker.go:239):
**Low (stats accuracy / question).** Tracing the rejection accounting: `rejected = (rawCount - len(validated)) + missingLabelSets` then `+= inserted.Excluded + inserted.Capped`, where `Excluded + Capped = len(validated) - Inserted`. So `mappings_returned - mappings_rejected = Inserted - missingLabelSets`, i.e. when a cell has label sets with no evidence (`missingLabelSets > 0`) the reported returned/rejected no longer reconcile to the number actually inserted, and missing label sets are counted as 'rejected mappings' even though they were never returned by the LLM. If that's intentional (missing-evidence label sets are deliberately folded into `rejected`), a one-line comment documenting the semantics would help; otherwise consider excluding `missingLabelSets` from `mappings_rejected` or tracking it as a separate stat. A small unit test pinning the arithmetic for a missing-label-set case would lock the intent either way.
