Comment (internal/service/worker/service.go:719):
**Nit (clarity).** `aiCfg ...*config.AIConfig` is a variadic that only ever carries 0 or 1 element (callers pass either nothing or a single `aiConfigFromConfig(...)`), purely to preserve the old signature. A variadic-as-optional-arg is a smell — it lets a caller pass two configs with no compile error and the body silently uses only `aiCfg[0]`. Prefer a plain `aiCfg *config.AIConfig` (nil when absent) and update the two call sites; it's clearer and forces callers to be explicit.
